issue_comments.body:
Rebased on current main, conflicts gone (they were in `Scheduler.__init__`, purely additive against the new `reset_preempted_req_ids`).

@hmellor your simplification is in. I kept the single predicate used directly at both sites, but flipped the name to match its polarity: the suggested code kept `terminal_stream_finish` for what is now the non-terminal condition, so it reads `stream_continues` (and `not in` instead of `not ... in`).

@y123456y78 both comments now state the constraint instead of narrating the old bug.

Mergeable again. Happy to get a `ready` label to kick CI.

@andylolu2 one change vs your suggestion. With `get_max_audio_tokens` = prefix, the encoder cache shrinks to `max(max_num_batched_tokens, 39)`. A paused session keeps its last chunk cached until it resumes (with async scheduling the last position is recomputed, so it can't be freed earlier), so at start each session pins ~41 embeds. With `--max-num-batched-tokens 256`, 12 sessions deadlock: 0/12 transcribed, main does 12/12.

So the subclass now only shrinks the profiling audio (`get_max_audio_array_len`) and keeps the item size at `max_model_len`, the encoder cache is the same as on main. Boot at `max_model_len` 131072 still OK, 12/12 at 256.

The encoder cache being sized only by `max(budget, item size)` is a core issue for streaming sessions in general, I can open an issue for it.
